  "key_findings": [
    "1. Tree-based methods (RF, XGB) are seed-stable on all splits (\u03c3_R\u00b2 < 0.01)",
    "2. XGBoost shows lowest mean error across all 3 splits (R\u00b2=0.986/0.905/0.648)",
    "3. MLP shows 200x variance amplification S1\u2192S3 (\u03c3: 0.001 \u2192 0.227)",
    "4. BNN shows 100x variance amplification S1\u2192S3 (\u03c3: 0.002 \u2192 0.192)",
    "5. BNN uncertainty is severely miscalibrated under shift",
    "   Predicted: 3.4%, Actual error: 39% (12x underestimate)",
    "6. PRIOR Draft 0 single-seed claim of \"MLP R\u00b2=0.04 on S3\" was a worst-case seed",
    "   Average is R\u00b2=0.54, but variance is hidden under single-seed evaluation"
  ],
  "implication_for_paper": "Variance amplification under shift constitutes a NEW finding: single-seed evaluation systematically underestimates deployment risk. Reframes paper from \"X is best\" to \"X is most reliable.\""
